[gd_scene format=3]

; The Calving, west of the Coldstacks (map offset (162.5, -71)): an ice cliff that sheds. From the Coldstacks' high
; doorway the pilgrim comes out on top of a cliff of old ice, 16 m over the floor, and drops (a hard landing wakes the
; Chorister asleep at the cliff's foot). Calved blocks of ice lie about the floor; west, the doorway on to the Bore.
; Back up the cliff: an iron girder frozen into its face (Mag-grip) or two mooring rings (Harpoon).

